OL,3,GNEWSAAlcoholic former GP saved by
OL,4,ASalvation Army
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former GP who spent six years of his
OL,7,Fcareer battling alcohol addiction, said
OL,8,Fhis life was saved by a treatment
OL,9,Fcentre run by The Salvation Army.
OL,11,FNicholas Lawrence, 65, said he was at
OL,12,Fthe end of his 40-year career when he
OL,13,F"ran into problems with alcohol" and
OL,14,Fdespite several attempts to get sober
OL,15,Fkept relapsing.
OL,17,FIt was only following a stay at the
OL,18,FSalvation Army's residential addictions
OL,19,Frecovery centre Gloucester House in
OL,20,FHighworth, Swindon, that he was able to
OL,21,Fstop drinking and has now been sober
OL,22,Ffor over a year.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,350,340,200,160,0,100
